<!--
	FrilArea7Challenge - Sandbox Option Presets
	Author: Frilioth
	Version: 3.0.1

	Puts Area 7's suggested settings in their OWN group in the Sandbox Options preset
	dropdown, alongside Difficulty / Official / User, instead of landing under "User".

	The group name comes from the "category" attribute on <area7_presets> below.
	Every <preset> in here appears inside that group.

	IMPORTANT: the game shows the group by looking up the localisation key
	  sandboxPresetGroup<category>
	so category="Area7" needs a "sandboxPresetGroupArea7" row in Localization.csv.
	Without it the dropdown shows the raw key instead of a friendly name.
	Keep the category a single word (no spaces) so the key stays tidy.

	HOW TO FILL IN A PRESET
	  1. In game: New Game -> Sandbox Options, set everything the way you want it.
	  2. Use the copy button next to the sandbox code box (left-hand panel) to copy the code.
	  3. Paste it into the code="" attribute of a preset below, replacing the placeholder.
	  4. Save this file and restart the game. No recompile needed.

	A preset whose code is still the placeholder is SKIPPED, so a half-finished entry
	will not show up broken in the menu.

	ATTRIBUTES
	  name             required. Internal id. No spaces.
	  code             required. The sandbox code copied from the options screen.
	  description      required (or description_key for a Localization.csv key).
	  localized_name   optional. What players actually see. Falls back to name.
	  icon             optional. NOT a ui_game_symbol_* sprite - a bare sprite name renders
	                   nothing. Two forms work:

	                     1. A vanilla resources path, e.g.
	                          icon="Data/Sandbox/icons/user_custom"
	                        (the artwork the game uses for user presets)

	                     2. YOUR OWN IMAGE from this mod folder, e.g.
	                          icon="@modfolder(FrilArea7Challenge):Resources/area7_preset.png"
	                        Put the PNG in the mod's Resources folder next to the .unity3d
	                        bundles. The menu draws this with an XUi <texture> element, which runs the
	                        path through the standard mod-path resolver and then loads it off
	                        disk - so an ordinary PNG in the mod works, no asset bundle needed.
	                        It is drawn at 180x180 and keeps its aspect ratio, so a square
	                        image is the safest choice.
	  difficulty_rating optional. Number shown as the preset's difficulty.
	  default          optional. "true" marks it as the default selection.

	DIFFICULTY LADDER
	  These presets are difficulty tiers, NOT per-world settings - the world is chosen
	  separately (Choose Area 7 (Biome)), so one ladder covers every biome.

	  difficulty_rating puts a skull and "xN" next to the preset in the menu. It is only
	  shown for non-user, non-custom presets, which ours are, so it will display.
	  Keep the numbers ascending or the ladder reads oddly.

	  Each tier needs its OWN code: set that tier up in Sandbox Options, copy the code,
	  paste it here. Tiers still holding the placeholder are skipped, so you can add them
	  one at a time and the finished ones still work.
-->

<area7_presets category="Area7">

	<preset name="Area7Recruit"
	        localized_name="Recruit"
	        description="Everything walks. Damage dialled right down. For learning the layout of Area 7 without dying to it."
	        difficulty_rating="1"
	        icon="@modfolder(FrilArea7Challenge):Resources/area7_preset_recruit.png"
	        code="AAPABADGFCGGCGECBDCAUAAMLBRDBFGBGGANBBJABKABLABNABPABOABVACIBCJBCDACEACAACFACHCCXBEABEXGFKAEPAEQAEUAEVAERAFLDFOD" />

	<preset name="Area7Grunt"
	        localized_name="Grunt"
	        description="Gentle but honest. Zombies jog at night, damage slightly below standard."
	        difficulty_rating="2"
	        icon="@modfolder(FrilArea7Challenge):Resources/area7_preset_grunt.png"
	        code="AAPABADBRDBFGANBBJABKBBLBBNABPABOABVACIBCDACEACAACFBCHCCXBEABEXGFKAEPAEQAEUAEVAERAFLFFOF" />

	<preset name="Area7Soldier"
